# =============================================================================
# spis_exclusions.tcl - coverage waivers for block 14, the SPI slave.
#
# Applied in IMC after loading the merged SPI slave run:
#     imc -exec flow/cov/spis_report.tcl
# or typed at the IMC prompt. Every line has its reason. Sign-off criterion 3
# (flow/0_signoff_criteria.md): code coverage 100% after the waivers below.
# Checked against JasperGold by ./flow/formal/unr_block.sh spis.
#
# Four reasons cover everything here:
#   1. No register of this block is wider than 9 bits, and bits 31, 28, 26, 24,
#      23, 21, 17 and 15 to 12 of ID (0x6A5D0E01) are 0: the read-data bits listed
#      are 0 in every register (SPIS section 6). Checked on every read by the
#      scoreboard.
#   2. PREADY is tied high (AHB2APB 7.5); checked by a_pready and a_shim_pready.
#   3. The SPI slave requests the DMA only for received bytes: the shim's
#      transmit-space input is tied low in garuda_spis_top.
#   4. The shim's two simulation-only checks cannot fire in a correct build.
# =============================================================================
exclude -inst garuda_spis_top -toggle prdata_o\[31\] -comment "read-data bit that is 0 in every register of this block (no register is wider than 9 bits and these bits of ID are 0): constant by specification, checked by the scoreboard on every read"
exclude -inst garuda_spis_top -toggle prdata_o\[28\] -comment "read-data bit that is 0 in every register of this block (no register is wider than 9 bits and these bits of ID are 0): constant by specification, checked by the scoreboard on every read"
